{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":5,"query":"name=Green&limit=10&title=Everything Is Tuberculosis","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"title":"Everything is tuberculosis ","subTitle":"the history and persistence of our deadliest infection "},{"@type":"alternative","title":"History and persistence of our deadliest infection"}],"name":[{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Green, John,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1977-"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJqk4KDvQPjXTWHWh8BwYP"},{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"Crash Course Books,","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"publisher"}}}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"still image"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"cartographic image"},{"@authority":"Medical Subject Headings","#text":"Popular Work"},{"@authority":"Medical Subject Headings","#text":"Personal Narrative"},{"@authority":"Répertoire de vedettes-matière","#text":"Récits personnels."},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Personal narratives"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Informational works."},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Illustrated works"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Documents d'information."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Récits personnels."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Ouvrages illustrés."},{"@authority":"sears","#text":"Informational works."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2025"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2025"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York, New York :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Crash Course Books, an imprint of Penguin Random House LLC,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":[2025]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"198 pages : illustrations, map, facsimiles ; 22 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"Tuberculosis has been entwined with humanity for millennia. Once romanticized as a malady of poets, today tuberculosis is seen as a disease of poverty that walks the trails of injustice and inequity we blazed for it. In 2019, author John Green met Henry Reider, a young tuberculosis patient at Lakka Government Hospital in Sierra Leone. John became fast friends with Henry, a boy with spindly legs and a big, goofy smile. In the years since that first visit to Lakka, Green has become a vocal advocate for increased access to treatment and wider awareness of the healthcare inequities that allow this curable, preventable infectious disease to also be the deadliest, killing over a million people every year. In Everything is Tuberculosis, John tells Henry's story, woven through with the scientific and social histories of how tuberculosis has shaped our world--and how our choices will shape the future of tuberculosis\"--Book jacket flap."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Introduction: Gregory and Stokes -- Lakka -- Cowboys and assassins -- Look at our railroads -- That wealth never warded off -- Whipped away -- Tiger got to hunt -- The flattering malady -- The bacillus -- Not a person -- A study in tuberculin -- Trepidation and hope -- The cure -- Where the cure is not -- Marco. Polo. -- Dr. Girum -- Henry -- \"Beat me later\" -- Superbug -- Vicious cycles -- Hail Mary -- Like magic -- Virtuous cycles -- The cause and the cure -- Postscript."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"John Green."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"f-sl---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Tuberculosis","History"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Tuberculosis","Social aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Tuberculosis","Treatment","History"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Tuberculosis","genre":"Popular works"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Medicine","History"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Social history"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Tuberculosis"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Tuberculosis, Pulmonary"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":["Tuberculosis, Pulmonary","history"]},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Social Conditions"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"History of Medicine"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Tuberculose"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Tuberculose","Aspect social"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Tuberculose","Histoire"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Histoire sociale"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Tuberculose","Traitement","Histoire"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Tuberculose","genre":"Ouvrages de vulgarisation"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Médecine","Histoire"]},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"social history"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"history of medicine"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SOCIAL SCIENCE / Disease & Health Issues"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"MEDICAL / Infectious Diseases"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / History"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Medicine"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Tuberculosis"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Tuberculosis","Treatment"]},{"@authority":"sears","topic":"Tuberculosis"},{"@authority":"lcsh","geographic":"Sierra Leone","topic":"Social conditions"},{"@authority":"mesh","geographic":"S